y} :question/id #uuid "2dbb8f8f-0f8e-5e43-b293-57a4173ad8a6" :question/math-academy-id "q-253241" :question/problem "Given that\n$D=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix},$\nfind $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi D}{6}\\right).$\n\n|  |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi D}{6}\\right)=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |  |\n|  |  | $0$ | $0$ | {{field-6}} |  |" :question/worked-solution "Given a function $f$ and a diagonal matrix $D$ with diagonal entries ${\\lambda }_{1},…,{\\lambda }_{n},$ we have\n\n$$\nf(D)=\\begin{bmatrix}f({\\lambda }_{1}) & ⋯ & 0 \\\\ ⋮ & ⋱ & ⋮ \\\\ 0 & ⋯ & f({\\lambda }_{n})\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{\\pi D}{6}\\right) & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{3\\pi }{6}\\right) & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{2\\pi }{6}\\right) & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\left(\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\\right)\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292546 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05588229-567c-5ebe-853e-4dda47b864e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290663}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "05588229-567c-5ebe-853e-4dda47b864e9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290663} :answer-field/id #uuid "265fe494-59f7-54cd-b50f-e009ee632de9" :answer-field/key "field-5" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291868} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4ce8a609-ad7b-5416-a7bf-3e2180618b1b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/re